    placement: each rectangle flush against exactly one corner (TL/TR/BL/BR)
  colors:
    moving_color: exactly one foreground color with 2-4 instances (the repeated color)
    singleton_colors: 0-2 other foreground colors, each appearing exactly once
    all distinct from bg and from each other
  constraints:
    grid >= 2s+1 in both dimensions (shifted rects stay in bounds)
    shifted moving rects must not overlap any singleton rect positions
  rule:
    moving rects are cleared and each translated diagonally inward by (s, s)
    direction per corner - TL:(+s,+s) TR:(+s,-s) BL:(-s,+s) BR:(-s,-s)
    singleton rects stay in place; same-color shifted rects may overlap (merge)

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick grid H x W where H,W >= 2s+1, s in [1,4]
    2. Assign 4 corners; pick how many are moving (2-4), rest are singletons
    3. Place shifted (output) moving rects at their inward positions (r+s,c+s from corner)
    4. Place singleton rects at their corners (unchanged in output)
    5. Verify no overlap between shifted moving rects and singletons
    6. Build input by moving each moving rect back to its corner and clearing shifted positions
